WEBVTT

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.090
I haven't seen Gure around.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.920
I wonder if he's still asleep.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.480
I wonder.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.950
I'll go check on him.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.870
Amore mangiare!

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.500
You're late, Gure.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.880
Hurry up and help open up shop.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.760
<b>Ichiotome</b>

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.110
These are some impressive strawberries.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.260
Where did you get these?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.290
Get this: I was on my morning run,

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.890
when I came across an old lady 
who had sprained her ankle.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.190
I took her to Shizuoka, and she let 
me pick some strawberries in return.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.820
All the way to Shizuoka?

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.500
That's a long ways.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.460
That good, huh?

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.260
These really are delicious.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.350
Aren't they?

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.200
I was floored when I had 
them over there, too.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.120
What's going on?

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.250
Hey, have some, Sui.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.780
They're really good.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.390
Freshly-picked strawberries.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.000
Yum!

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.430
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:46.390
<b>"Sweets Trap Collection"</b>

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.850
One chiffon, one anmitsu, please.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.220
All right.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.860
Oh yeah, do you remember that 
baked chocolat we had at Velico?

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.770
Yeah, Velico never disappoints.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:10.710
It was great.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:14.120
It's really hard to make them that moist.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:17.710
Oh yeah, and East Side Grande's eclairs.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.540
Oh yeah, those <i>crrrrrispy</i> ones.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.020
Yeah.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.840
You wouldn't think eclairs would be crispy.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:23.960
Nah, man.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.100
<i>Crrrrrispy</i>.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.680
Yeah, <i>crrrrrispy</i>, right?

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.190
<i>Crrrrrispy.</i>

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.360
<i>Crrrrrispy</i>.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.090
Gure, we're down to our last chiffon.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:43.740
Gotcha.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:47.200
Last chiffon.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.270
Okay.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:49.370
Pardon me.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.980
Yes, on my way.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.170
May I have a green tea chiffon and a blend?

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.170
Understood.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.790
Pardon me.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.470
Yes?

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.480
May I take your order?

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.720
I'd like two caffè lattes 
and a green tea chiffon.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.420
I'm sorry, we just sold out of chiffon cakes.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:18.940
Aw, you don't have the fluffy stuff?

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.340
What can we do?

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.810
Let's have something else.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:25.660
Hey, if you'd like, you 
can have my chiffon cake.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.000
May I order a matcha roll instead?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.620
Are you sure, though?

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.440
Yes.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.240
I was having a hard time deciding.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:34.540
Don't worry about it.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.300
Sorry. Thank you.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:38.920
You, too. Say thank you.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.820
Thank you.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.380
You're welcome.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:45.300
So you're switching to a matcha roll?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:46.620
Yes.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.550
Um, sir...

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:55.500
Yes?

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.110
Thank you for your kindness earlier.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:00.080
Can we thank you somehow?

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.860
Nah, don't worry about it.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.800
Are you the patissier?

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.070
Y-Yes.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.590
The matcha roll cake was delicious.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.770
Th-Thank you.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:13.080
I think it passes.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.080
Oh, you don't need to thank me,

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:20.090
but there might be something 
I'd like to ask you to do.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.470
I'd like you to participate in an 
event at the department store.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.310
That's a good response.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:35.310
Apologies for the late introduction.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:39.840
My name is Tsunozaki.
I'm an agent for the event.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:46.160
There's going to be a one-week exclusive 
sweets collection next week.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.030
One of the stores is
suddenly unable to attend,

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.490
so we've been looking for an alternative.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:53.800
Okay...

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.730
And your cake was delicious,

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:59.330
so I thought it'd be nice 
to have Rokuhoudou join.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:04.240
There'll be a café space, so you 
should be able to work as usual.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.930
But that would mean we'd have 
to close shop in the meantime.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.300
Yes, well...

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.430
A week, huh?

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.060
That's a bit long.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.120
Of course, I'm not demanding.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:22.300
It's just that it's going to take a long 
time for me to find another shop again.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.570
Could we do just three days?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:30.590
We have guests that look 
forward to spending time here.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.570
We can't stay closed for 
any longer than that.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:36.660
If that's good enough, we'd like to join.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.160
I see.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.240
I'm up for that.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:41.970
Me, too.

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:42.620
Yes.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.420
How's that?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.120
All right.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.630
Let's ask for three days.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.290
The details are written here.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:54.930
Please take a look through it.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:55.430
Okay.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.120
U-Um...

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:00.910
Is it an open kitchen?

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.520
I'm not good at working in front of people.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:08.990
It was closed off when I checked.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:10.830
Oh, good.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:15.540
Well, even though it's a department 
store event, it's a modest one.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.160
There's no reason to be intimidated.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.790
I see.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.540
Well, then.

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.580
I'll see you again on the day of the event.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.510
This is the event...?

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.070
We're really doing it here?

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.680
Oh, hello, everyone.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:40.930
Tsunozaki-san!

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.980
This isn't modest at all!

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.520
All the other places here are big names!

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.860
And it's really out in the open.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.440
Eh, this is still modest, no?

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:56.740
Well, Chocolatier Velico
was supposed to be in this spot.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.190
Velico?!

00:07:58.190 --> 00:07:59.620
<i>The</i> Velico?!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:03.830
Who would have thought we were 
called in place of that brand name?

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:07.000
And about the kitchen...

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.140
Oh, yeah, it's closed off, see?

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.590
I mean, it is, but...

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.760
I'm sure you'll be fine, Rokuhoudou.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.140
I look forward to it.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.030
See you.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.480
Nope, nope, nope, nope!

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.310
I can't work there!

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:33.500
That kitchen is going to be 
pretty rough for Tsubaki-kun.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:36.200
Don't worry, though, Tsubaki-kun.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.350
I'll make my latte art again if need be.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.110
And I'll work my pottery wheel.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:42.200
That has nothing to do with sweets!

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:45.360
Well, all the other shops are well-known.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.680
We aren't going to get 
hammered right off the bat.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.820
Right.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.380
They're going to go for them, first.

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:55.760
You're right, they won't be coming to 
a little-known store like ours first.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.390
I'm sure the customers will 
be making their rounds.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.770
Yeah.

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:04.120
With all those brand name shops there, people 
are going to have a lot of shopping to do.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:08.400
Well, then, let's just work 
at our own pace as usual.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:09.600
Okay.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:13.960
This looks good.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.150
Wow, let's go.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.550
Are we there yet?

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:17.660
Almost.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.290
Wait...

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.660
Huh? Is this our line?

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.330
No way.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.120
This must be for Lumierre across from us.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.920
Guys, big news! Look at this!

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:29.920
<b>Highly whispered-about shop tucked away by the port 
Rokuhoudou opening for just three days!</b>

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.110
When did they get these photos?

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:38.030
"Highly whispered-about shop?"

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.800
"The legendary top-quality café?"

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.350
Gure's is practically photoshopped.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.970
Huh? That looks right, doesn't it?

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.310
Dude, wait...

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:52.150
<b>Sweets specialist Nakao Tsubaki
Behold the masterful handiwork of the young 
patissier who keeps Rokuhoudou popular with all ages!</b>

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:52.150
"Behold the masterful handiwork 
of the young patissier"?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:55.820
Why are they pushing for Rokuhoudou so much?

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:01.580
Teehee.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:05.450
<i>Ah, it's Tsunozaki-san's doing.</i>

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.610
A-Anyway, we don't have a choice.

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:10.110
Let's do this, guys.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:10.830
Right.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.160
I'm going home!

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.420
Wait, Tsubaki-kun!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.040
This is madness!

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.850
This is so fun.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.320
They're so fun to mess with.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.310
Well, then...

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.030
Now that they've been bolstered so hugely,

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.700
it's up to those four whether they 
disappoint everyone or become famous.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.490
Let's see what you're made of.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:36.690
<b>Welcome to Rokuhoudou!!</b>

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.980
Three daifuku mochi and two 
matcha and chocolate tarts.

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:43.370
Enjoy.

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.960
Pardon me.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.040
Yes, coming.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.120
Me next, please.

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:49.600
Right.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:55.050
<b>Sasada
Inoue 
Matsumoto 
Suzuki 
Miyazaki 
Kayama 
Kagami 
Niuki 
Matsuda 
Honda</b>

00:10:55.050 --> 00:11:04.050
<b>Suzuki 
Takahashi 
Tanada 
Iikura 
Tezuka 
Murakami 
Natsume 
Mishima 
Akatsuka</b>

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.820
<i>I can't believe...</i>

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.050
<i>...that we're this busy.</i>

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.330
<i>We need to get on track somehow.</i>

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:06.750
I'll take over for a while.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:07.510
Please.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:08.520
Excuse me.

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.180
Yes.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:12.940
Can you do more daifukus?

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:13.820
Right.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:19.790
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.570
<i>Why?</i>

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:25.040
<i>Why are there so many people watching?!</i>

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.780
Tsubaki-kun, can you do the parfait first?

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:30.330
Um...

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:31.460
Um...

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.820
<i>Which one was it?</i>

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:43.300
How the hell do I do it again?!

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:46.900
Tsubaki-kun.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:49.570
Look.

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:49.850
It's so good!

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:55.210
This rare cheesecake is 
so rich. It's amazing.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:56.860
The mousse melts in your mouth.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.570
The anko goes so great with 
the bitterness of the tea.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.400
It's so fragrant, too.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:10.590
<i>Tsubaki-san.</i>

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:13.790
<i>It sure is as tasty as always.</i>

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:16.610
It's the same.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:18.920
It's same here as at Rokuhoudou.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.230
Yup.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:23.090
It's your sweets that are 
making it so, Tsubaki-kun.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:26.320
Our customers' smiles are 
the source of our strength.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.430
Sorry.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.570
I'm okay now.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.180
I'm going to pick up the pace.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:41.570
Here.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:43.860
I'll make more if we run out.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:45.520
Okay.

00:12:46.130 --> 00:12:48.900
Was it twenty roll cakes, next?

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.160
Yes, thank you.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.370
Sold out
 Rokuhoudou

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.300
That was exhausting.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:03.490
We're never so busy non-stop.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.550
Tsubaki-kun is beat, too.

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.080
He was going full-steam until we sold out.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.520
What shall we do tomorrow?

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.400
Tsubaki-kun?

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:19.290
T-Tomorrow...

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:19.990
What's wrong, Tsubaki-kun?

00:13:20.930 --> 00:13:24.490
The café menu for tomorrow...

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:26.410
What about the café menu?

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:30.700
Wait, what were you saying?!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.160
Tsubaki-kun, wake up, please.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.000
At least tell us about the menu.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:35.490
Tsubaki-kun!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.490
Tsubaki-kun!

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:36.860
Come home to us!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:36.860
Tsubaki-kun!

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:37.370
Tsubaki-kun!

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.760
Tsubaki-kun!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:44.000
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.040
Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori.

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:50.100
Strawberry shortcakes and strawberry tarts!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.650
And then they have strawberry 
daifukus and strawberry anmitsu.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.140
They even have roll cakes.

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.680
They didn't have strawberry 
items on the menu yesterday.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.390
I know.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:13:59.550
Strawberries are great.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:01.320
I'm so hyped.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:03.530
Daily menus, huh?

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:06.530
<b>Rokuhoudou Special
 Today Only
 Strawberries Galore Menu!!!</b>

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:05.490
Not bad.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.700
<b>Strawberry Tarts

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:08.700
I'd like this one and this one.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.360
Right away.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:11.280
Excuse me.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:12.530
Coming.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.670
I'd like a strawberry daifuku.

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:16.000
Understood.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.880
One strawberry parfait and 
one strawberry anmitsu.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.090
Tsubaki-kun.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.090
Let's plow through this.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.890
I got this.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:37.480
<i>Although there are more people watching 
me than there were yesterday.</i>

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:46.490
<i>I make sweets.</i>

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.290
<i>I make sweets.</i>

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:52.950
<i>I make sweets.</i>

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:55.700
Tsubaki-kun's turned on.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.000
Yum!

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.130
What the heck? 
These strawberries are so good!

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:04.570
The sweet-sour flavor fills your mouth.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.550
This is rejuvenating.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:10.010
<i>I wasn't sure we'd make it yesterday,</i>

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:14.320
<i>but it looks like we're 
getting the hang of it.</i>

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:16.450
<i>We might just make it.</i>

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:17.850
Hey...

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:20.380
The strawberries were really good.

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.190
Do you have business cards?

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:24.560
Yes, thank you.

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:29.650
Please visit us here someday.

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.280
We'll be waiting.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.280
I'm so glad we got this.

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:36.580
We should totally go.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.420
Wait, Tsunozaki-san, what did you just say?

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:50.420
I want you to take part in the TV interview.

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:55.970
But today's our last day here.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.350
I don't know what we could 
do with the introductions.

00:15:57.700 --> 00:15:58.990
Why not?

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:01.430
It'll be good advertising for you.

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:03.500
You were kind enough to 
participate in the event.

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.400
At least let me do this for you.

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:07.110
In fact...

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:10.240
I've already given them the 
go-ahead, so please and thank you.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.990
Please and thank you.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.610
<b>Sweets Shop Rokuhoudou</b>

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:16.870
I'm at Rokuhoudou's booth here.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:18.530
Hello.

00:16:19.030 --> 00:16:20.540
Hello.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:25.040
You even get to see the 
sweets-making in action.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.170
What are you working on now?

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.920
Is there something you keep 
in mind when you make the anko?

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.090
Do you make mochi here, too?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.300
How many do you make in a day?

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:37.300
<i>I'm not emotionally prepared.</i>

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.560
<i>I can't explain anything!</i>

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:42.750
Here, just have a bite.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:50.440
This is so...

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:54.640
The fluffy hanamame goes so well 
with the chewiness of the mochi!

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:58.560
Also, this is the cake that 
we served at the café today.

00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:59.330
Please.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.460
May I?!

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:04.750
This cake looks great, too!

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:05.870
Let's see...

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:13.970
Now, let's hear from the manager, too.

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:15.000
Okay.

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.740
You look quite young.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.630
Are you the founder of the café?

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:22.810
No, it was originally my 
grandfather's business.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.780
I inherited it.

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:26.480
I see.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:28.270
Oh, and also...

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:33.150
I've heard that you're related 
to a large corporation.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:37.350
How did you know about that?

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.590
Um...

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.290
W-Well...

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.040
I'm surprised you knew.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:49.120
Tokitaka-kun.

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:50.260
Speaking of which,

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:54.440
did you know that there's an 
even bigger secret to our shop?

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.770
Why don't I show you, then...

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:08.940
The oasis of my soul and 
Rokuhoudou's good luck cat...

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.880
Kinako!

00:18:12.930 --> 00:18:14.650
So cute!

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:18.770
Unfortunately, today is the last day 
that we participate in the event.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:22.550
We have all sorts of menus at our shop.

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:24.660
Please visit us.

00:18:24.850 --> 00:18:26.430
We'll be waiting.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:27.380
Okay!

00:18:27.380 --> 00:18:29.460
Wait, they shut me down!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:30.630
Oh, well!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.700
That's it from Rokuhoudou.

00:18:35.650 --> 00:18:37.300
Thank you.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.300
No problem.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.300
He managed to dodge the question...

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.680
Thank you for taking time 
out of your busy schedule.

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.930
Thank you for your business.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:48.270
We can finally go back to our normal lives.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.580
Good job.

00:18:49.580 --> 00:18:54.870
Hey, isn't that Tsunozaki-san 
from East Side Grande?

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:55.940
He is!

00:18:56.290 --> 00:18:59.560
The rising star of western 
sweets and prodigal patissier.

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.920
He's so fine.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.950
I wish he'd give me an autograph.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.720
What?!

00:19:07.720 --> 00:19:11.080
The <i>crrrrrispy</i> guy?!

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.500
Good work, everyone.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:16.410
Thank you for all your 
work the past three days.

00:19:16.410 --> 00:19:19.230
I got to learn all about you. It was fun.

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:21.610
I'd like to come down to your place again.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:23.640
Sure, we'll be waiting for you.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:25.890
Well then, let's meet again.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:30.640
Give him a call for once,

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:32.880
little brother.

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.490
What did he just say?

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:40.690
Little brother?

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:47.350
<i>Did he know about me all along?</i>

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:04.510
I'm back, Kyou-kun.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:11.520
I had lots of fun watching 
the people at Rokuhoudou.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:18.070
Though, I ended up only 
helping advertise them.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:23.720
I tried to get your younger
brother, Kyousui-kun,

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:27.550
to fess up, but he dodged me.

00:20:27.930 --> 00:20:32.290
It seems your brother doesn't want 
to talk about his family, does he?

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:36.750
I don't remember asking you to pry.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.620
It's just a personal fascination.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:44.050
I'm curious why your brother has such 
a hard time getting along with you.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:47.720
It's so funny, he has the same face as you,

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.790
but he makes so many expressions.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:51.290
That's a twin for you.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:53.570
Hey.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:56.630
Isn't your shop going to be in 
the event starting tomorrow?

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:58.800
You'd better be well-prepared.

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:00.800
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:05.610
I'll work my butt off not to 
shame the almighty Tougoku Group.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:08.190
Tougoku Yakyou-san.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:22.770
You're still running that shop, Kyousui?

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:39.340
Yakyou...

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:30.090
<b>Next episode</b>

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:30.090
<b>"Tempura Bowl Survivor"
"Incident Meow"</b>

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.570
Sampling apparently makes 
things taste even better

00:23:18.570 --> 00:23:23.360
because you have just a small portion 
at a place where you don't normally eat.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:27.690
So then eating takoyaki in bed 
in the morning must be the best.

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:30.090
<b>Come again soon.</b>

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:29.240
Uh, sure.
